Why Is Demand Increasing
Rising Global Protein Demand: Growing middle-class consumption in Asia and Africa is increasing seafood demand and encouraging fishing fleets and processors to expand capacity and improve operational efficiency.
Modernization of Fishing Fleets: Satellite navigation, AI-driven stock assessment, automated net systems, GPS, and fleet-management technologies are helping operators improve route planning, fuel efficiency, catch management, and compliance.
Expansion of Cold-Chain and Premium Seafood: Improved cold-chain infrastructure is supporting higher-value export channels, particularly for premium species, while traceability and certification are strengthening access to retail and foodservice buyers.

Commercial Fishing Watch: Sustainability, Digital Tracking and Marketplaces
The commercial fishing industry is increasingly adopting digital tools for vessel monitoring, electronic logbooks, catch reporting, and stock assessment. Sustainability certifications such as MSC and ASC are also becoming increasingly important in buyer relationships. At the same time, API-driven B2B marketplaces are creating new channels for connecting fishers, distributors, and buyers while improving price transparency.

